{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\nowidctlpar\f0\fs24 Ms. Elwin reviewed the agenda item along with the staff recommendation. No comments were received from the public. In response to Vice Chair Bays\rquote inquiry, Ms. Elwin explained how the Citrus County transit funds could be used. Vice Chair Bays expressed her support for transit services but also shared her concern that many Citrus County residents are living at or below the poverty level, moving to lower-cost rural areas where providing transit services is more challenging, and that transit services warrant a broader discussion. Chair Allocco concurred, noting that transit services tend to be more effective in urban areas, while rural areas are less likely to receive comparable service, and acknowledged the challenge of making transit financially feasible for taxpayers and potential users. Ms. Elwin reminded the Board that the annual review of each county\rquote s Transit Development Plan would be forthcoming and that the respective Boards of County Commissioners would soon have an opportunity to receive an update on the annual performance of their transit systems.\f1\par
\pard\cf1\par
}

