\viewkind4\uc1\pard\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li360\cf1\f0\fs24\'b7\tab\f1 Councilman Hallal inquired about the process for pressure washing the Good Neighbor Trail bridge at US 50 and Jefferson, as well as the steps that will be taken to prevent continued rusting on the bridge pillars. Suzanne Ziegler, District 7 Liaison for the Florida Department of Transportation (FDOT), provided the contact information for Tyler Mathews, Brooksville Operations Engineer, to both Councilman Hallal and Richard Weeks, Brooksville Public Works Director.\f2\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\f0\'b7\tab\f1 Councilman Davis expressed concern about the increasing misuse of e-bikes and asked whether any state funding was available to support public awareness efforts for e-bike users. Chair Allocco noted that relevant legislation had been passed but later vetoed. Ms. Ziegler agreed with the need for public awareness and stated she would reach out to the FDOT Public Information Office to determine whether any resources already exist. She also mentioned that funding for education could be included in the MPO\rquote s Unified Planning Work Program. Chair Allocco suggested that the counties could consider installing educational signage in areas experiencing the most issues. \i [Subsequent to the meeting, Ms. Ziegler provided contact information for Safe Kids Suncoast, the organization that FDOT District 7 partners with to provide safety education in local schools. For additional coordination or information, please contact Sheila Rainey at \cf2\ul srainey5@jh.edu <mailto:srainey5@jh.edu>\cf1\ulnone .]\par
\i0\f0\'b7\tab\f1 Chair Allocco recognized and thanked outgoing Commissioners Bays and Campbell for their dedicated service to Citrus and Hernando counties and to the MPO Board.\cf3\f2\par
}

